# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# project-planning/.gitignore — artifact durability tiering
#
# Tier 1 (durable record) is TRACKED — it is the intent → decisions
# → outcome story a future run or reader needs.
# Tiers 2-4 are working material: produced and read by the pipeline
# DURING a run, superseded by shipped code + ADRs + the ship report.
#
# gitignore != delete. Every ignored file still exists on disk and is
# still written/read by the pipeline exactly as before. Nothing about
# what a stage PRODUCES changes — only what survives as the committed
# documentation surface.
#
# Contract: .agent/manifests/README.md § "Artifact durability tiers"
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Tier 2 — compiler output (mechanically extracted from the spec)
specs/*-minimal-*.md
PRD/*-minimal-*.md

# Tier 3 — run-scoped working material
plans/task-breakdown-*.md
plans/qa-report.md
plans/qa-report-*.md
plans/code-review-*.md
plans/test-report-*.md
architecture/
brain-dumps/
ui-design/
design-prototypes/

# Tier 4 — mutable machine state
# (byte-identical to the latest workflow/run-<id>.json, which IS tracked;
#  "which run is live" is derivable as latest-by-timestamp — the fallback
#  /status already implements)
workflow/current-run.json

# Retired destination — no longer written to by any stage.
# Pre-existing contents stay on disk and in git history.
archive/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRACKED BY OMISSION (deliberate — this is the durable record):
#   specs/{prd,frd,bug}-NNN.md   ADR/            baseline.md
#   STATUS.md                    tasks.md        smoke/
#   plans/ship-report-*.md       captures/       spike-notes/
#   plans/*probe-findings*.md    source-analysis/
#   workflow/run-*.json
#
# NOTE: plans/ is deliberately NOT ignored wholesale. The three transient
# families are named individually so ship reports and probe findings stay
# tracked — a negation pattern could not rescue them, because git cannot
# un-ignore a file inside an ignored directory.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
